{"id":20685,"artist":"Mic Darling.","title":"Carrigfergus","lyrics_plain":null,"lyrics_synced":"[00:01.61] I wish I was in Carrigfergus,\n[00:10.56] Only for nights in Ballygrant,\n[00:18.45] I would swim over the deepest ocean,\n[00:27.40] For my love to find.\n[00:35.30] But the sea is wide and I cannot cross over,\n[00:43.98] And neither have I wings to fly.\n[00:52.14] I wish I could meet a handsome boatsman,\n[01:01.09] To ferry me over, to my love and die.\n[01:10.00] My childhood days bring back sad reflections,\n[01:18.95] Of happy times I spent so long ago.\n[01:26.84] My boyhood friends and my own relations,\n[01:35.79] Have all passed on now like melting snow.\n[01:43.68] But I'll spend my days in endless roaming,\n[01:52.37] Soft is the grass, my bed is free.\n[02:00.53] Ah, to be back now in Carrigfergus,\n[02:09.47] On that long road down to the sea.\n[02:17.37] But in Kilkenny, it is reported\n[02:26.32] On marble stones there as black as ink.\n[02:34.21] With gold and silver I would support her,\n[02:43.16] But I'll sing no more 'till I get a drink.\n[02:51.05] For I'm drunk today, and I'm seldom sober,\n[02:59.74] A handsome rover from town to town.\n[03:07.89] Ah, but I'm sick now, my days are numbered,\n[03:16.84] Come all you young men and lay me down.\n[03:25.26] Come all you young men and lay me down.\n","lyrics_synced_enhanced":"[00:01.61] <00:01.61>I <00:02.13>wish <00:02.92>I <00:03.19>was <00:05.82>in <00:06.34>Car <00:06.87>rig <00:07.40>fer <00:07.92>gus,\n[00:10.55] <00:10.55>On <00:10.82>ly <00:11.08>for <00:11.61>nights <00:14.24>in <00:14.76>Bal <00:15.55>ly <00:15.82>grant,\n[00:18.45] <00:18.45>I <00:18.98>would <00:19.76>swim <00:20.03>o <00:20.55>ver <00:22.66>the <00:23.19>deep <00:23.71>est <00:24.24>o <00:24.76>cean,\n[00:27.40] <00:27.40>For <00:27.92>my <00:28.45>love <00:32.40>to <00:32.66>find.\n[00:35.29] <00:35.29>But <00:35.55>the <00:35.82>sea <00:36.34>is <00:36.87>wide <00:39.50>and <00:39.76>I <00:40.03>can <00:40.55